From f11a08ab60e5c7f05f96caa2783655dc89f3d969 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <teste@hemofilia.org.br>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:03:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 41/41] dock: Moves the Dock and Clip like Window Maker, and
 adds the launcher menu.

Dock and Clip can be dragged to another corner of the output: Edge
left/right by the horizontal half, anchor top/bottom by the vertical half
the pointer is released in; a horizontal dock keeps its orientation. The
Clip previews the corner while dragging; its dock-apps follow. The Dock
(the layer surface of namespace 'wlmdock') is dragged by the compositor:
Beyond a threshold of 8 pixels, wlmdock loses the pointer and does not
launch. Dock and Clip don't share a corner: The other one takes the moved
one's former corner. The new Edge and Anchor are stored in the state file,
and wlmdock re-reads its position on SIGUSR1, which wlmaker sends. The
Clip's menu has items to move it to the other side or end, too.

wlmdock gets a right-click menu for launchers, drawn on its surface which
grows for it: Launch, Kill (processes it launched), Remove (stored in the
state; for the Clip's launchers, wlmdock signals wlmaker to update the room
it leaves), and moving the Dock to the other side or end (not into the
Clip's corner). It closes when the pointer leaves the surface, or on a
click elsewhere. Areas without content are transparent now, not black.
'wlmdock --clip' uses the layer namespace 'wlmdock-clip'.

Unit tests for the quadrant to Edge/Anchor mapping, the corner conflict
resolution and the Edge/Anchor plist coding.
